{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, I’ve been vomiting all day and can’t keep anything down—not even water. It’s been like this since this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have a history of gastroparesis, right? Is this similar to your past episodes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly like before. But this time, I stopped taking my Reglan because the pharmacy didn’t have the generic, and my insurance wouldn’t cover the brand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could definitely make things worse. Not taking your metoclopramide likely contributed to this flare-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so that’s why I’m feeling so bad again? I didn’t realize it was that important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It really is. It helps your stomach empty properly. We’ll get you back on it right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ve also been feeling really dizzy and my heart’s racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s probably from dehydration. Your heart rate was elevated when you arrived. We’re giving you IV fluids to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that makes sense. I haven’t had anything to drink all day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve also started you on anti-nausea medications—Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan—to help settle your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken Compazine at home before. It helps a little, but not completely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re using a combination now to get better control. Your labs show your blood sugar was high—330—when you came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it’s been hard to manage when I can’t eat. I didn’t know how much insulin to take."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. We’ve lowered your Lantus dose temporarily because you’re not eating much. We’ll adjust it as you start tolerating food again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. Should I still take my sliding scale insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep the sliding scale. The diabetes team will help fine-tune it as your intake improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my blood pressure? I’ve been off my clonidine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned you stopped it because you weren’t sure if it was safe with lisinopril?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I thought maybe they were too similar. I didn’t want to drop my pressure too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They work differently, so it’s safe to take both. We’re restarting the clonidine patch today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I’m glad to hear that. I’ve had high readings at home lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor it closely. Your exam shows no abdominal pain, and your liver tests are normal, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No pain, just the nausea and vomiting. I’m just so tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-05-16 18:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with dehydration and poor intake. The fluids should help you feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. I haven’t vomited since last night, and I sipped some ginger ale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’re going to try advancing your diet—start with toast and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat regular food soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go step by step. If toast goes well, we’ll try soup later. We also gave you a handout on a gastroparesis-friendly diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll make sure it fits with my diabetes plan too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your blood sugar was 145 this morning—much better. We’ll keep adjusting your insulin as you eat more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m worried about it spiking once I start eating again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-05-17 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help you manage that. Your Lantus dose will go back up gradually. Follow the sliding scale we provided."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-05-17 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your heart rate has normalized, and labs show your hydration is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-05-17 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-05-17 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep tolerating food and fluids, yes. We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. You’re stable and tolerating toast and ginger ale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue taking your metoclopramide four times a day. If nausea returns, use Compazine as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow the sliding scale. As your eating improves, you may need to increase your Lantus—call your doctor to adjust it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Any other instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep your follow-up with your gastroenterologist in two months. If symptoms return or you have pacer concerns, go to their clinic any afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I remember that from last time. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, if you develop fever, chest pain, or trouble breathing, seek help right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’m just glad to be feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home with a prescription for metoclopramide—make sure you get the generic this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned my lesson there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Take it slow with your diet, stay hydrated, and keep up with your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2197-05-18 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed, but I hope you stay on track."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-05-16 18:25:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-05-18 14:55:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer, and hypertension was admitted for nausea and vomiting, unable to tolerate oral intake. The flare was attributed to discontinuation of metoclopramide due to lack of generic prescription coverage. She was treated with IV fluids, antiemetics, and restarted on metoclopramide, leading to symptom improvement. Her insulin regimen was adjusted due to reduced oral intake, and she was restarted on clonidine for blood pressure control after clarifying safety with lisinopril. She advanced to tolerating toast and ginger ale, with stable vital signs and improved hydration. She was discharged home with updated medication instructions, a gastroparesis diet handout, and follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Other postprocedural status",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
